{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/bot_surfaces/tests.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T06:06:30.833707Z","id":"11cc73fe811ed22dccbaa76d7d2ccd1e081ac1bf93b5ed09720b2ac829b5a0ae","body":{"detail":"generated(seed, steps) mixes Accepted, errors, results and RetryAfter in random orders and serves (bot_surfaces/tests.rs, `retry: Retry::NONE` near line 2694), the fixture replay (Replay, near line 257) and crates/clax-server/tests/api_bot_surfaces.rs (`retry: Retry::NONE` in Daemon) likewise. Run under Retry::DAEMON with an invariant 'an accepted call of an @once operation is never delivered again', the generator would have found the one-serve `accepted` then retryable error case recorded as a blocker on bot_surfaces.rs:2611:2620.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":2477},"end":{"line":2480},"content_hash":"e69cbd4d699f94945138b37ca86ff2c1282f56c092c0eb8c0d9e918dce79931f"},"summary":"The generated sequences of answers, the fixture's replay and the HTTP daemon test all open their calls under `Retry::NONE`, so none of them exercises sending again","tags":["claxbot-surfaces","retries","tests","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/bot_surfaces/tests.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T06:55:23.394011Z","id":"925a7d3dab7ab7b9c4fbd9469e312c6ed8bb9da969f8d0ba766a0df5f0b7b8df","body":{"detail":"16 seeds x 2000 steps on the hub's clock; Seen { again: 481, accepted_then_failed: 836, settled: 8037 } at the time it was written; about 7 s with the older generator. It fails on the pre-5fe1294a6 hub. Not changed: the fixture replay and crates/clax-server/tests/api_bot_surfaces.rs still open calls under Retry::NONE.","kind":"comment","references":"11cc73fe811ed22dccbaa76d7d2ccd1e081ac1bf93b5ed09720b2ac829b5a0ae","summary":"Done for the hub in eb641ecb6: `retrying(seed, steps)` and no_sequence_of_calls_sent_again_breaks_what_sending_again_promises run calls under Retry::DAEMON (some NONE) with restarts, away hosts and going on, holding @once-accepted never resent, nothing sent settled or at its deadline, same ID/key/run/args on every send, settled exactly once","tags":["session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/bot_surfaces/tests.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T22:47:15.583460Z","id":"68e9e5837b009ea1ac8bcc9c858fc448ff518026fa6fe5d5ce43812c6f475edc","body":{"detail":"retrying() (crates/clax-bot/src/bot_surfaces/tests.rs:3212-3512) restarts by building a new Hub over the same MemoryPending (3281-3291), which does rebuild every hub-side state from the store and would catch state kept only in the hub. But the rules it asserts about attempts ('attempts given back', 'past its rule', 'past the run's bound', 3478-3500) read store.tries_of and store.resends, the same numbers the hub wrote; Tracked::sent, the host-observed count, is incremented (3473) and never compared with anything. The send-safety invariants (never after settled, never at or after the deadline, never an accepted @once ask, sent as made: 3451-3469) are from the deliveries and are sound. MemoryHub (crates/clax-testkit/src/fake_host/memory.rs) also uses MemoryPending, so none of the retries.rs tests exercise StoredPending's Tries conversion (tries_of/kept_tries, crates/clax-bot/src/broker/stored.rs:257-292), call_resends' SQL sum or mark_sent/accept_call's SQL; the SQLite path has a few integration tests (crates/clax-bot/tests/outside.rs a_call_in_its_attempts_outlasts_a_restart_of_the_daemon) and one store test of keep_call_tries (crates/clax-store/src/bot_pending.rs around 3732). The two Pending implementations agree today as far as reading them shows (open_call rule, sent_calls/mark_sent, accept_call, keep_tries, resends), but nothing would notice if they drifted.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":3478},"end":{"line":3500},"content_hash":"92dfcb80555af19432c597d64de56da8fe83d80560c2b9e50cbe8147aa0af71a"},"suggested_fix":"Run the same drawn sequences over StoredPending on a temporary Store (opening calls through BrokerStore::open_placed under a claimed run), restarting with a new Hub over the same Store, and assert per call that the number of separate sendings after a failure seen by the host never exceeds the rule's attempts.","summary":"The generator's restarts and every retries.rs test run over MemoryPending only; its attempt invariants check the store's bookkeeping, not the sends a host saw","tags":["review","review:claxbot-surfaces-deep","fix-regression","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/bot_surfaces/tests.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-13T00:20:51.048821Z","id":"056a4de6fd4e22434fa3a760433e57cdd6eebae8dfeae14c6580943ef5fbcf61","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-bot/src/bot_surfaces/tests.rs: retrying() is generic over a Played store (MemoryPending, and StoredPending on a store on disk, whose runs are made, claimed and begun and whose calls are opened at their places through crate::broker::enqueue_placed, as a driver opens them; a restart is a new Hub and a new StoredPending over the same Store). New invariants from the deliveries: a call is delivered after a retryable failure (Tracked::again) fewer times than its rule's attempts, and a run's calls of a registration no more often in all than resends_per_run; some call is delivered twice. Tests: no_sequence_of_calls_sent_again_breaks_what_sending_again_promises (16 seeds, memory) and no_sequence_of_calls_sent_again_breaks_what_sending_again_promises_in_the_store (3 seeds x 1,200 steps over the store; both together 4.3 s). crates/clax-testkit/src/fake_host/retries.rs: every test whose hub desk_with makes (26 of 27; an_old_host_is_served_as_before_rules_were_given builds its own) runs as <name>::in_memory and <name>::in_the_store, the latter over MemoryHub::in_the_store (crates/clax-testkit/src/fake_host/memory.rs: StoredPending on a home of its own, restart() makes a new adapter over the same store); the restart, lease-ended and retry_after_ms tests among them. //crates/clax-testkit:clax_testkit_lib_test 75 passed.","kind":"comment","references":"68e9e5837b009ea1ac8bcc9c858fc448ff518026fa6fe5d5ce43812c6f475edc","summary":"Done, not closed here: the generator and the fake host's retry tests run over StoredPending too, and the generator holds what the host was sent","tags":["fix:second-pass","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
